Exactly. The bucket supplies shape, capacity, and constraints. What fills it determines its present function.

Pantheon’s symbols and modules are buckets. Context, evidence, intent, sensory input, and action fill them. The same bucket can hold research, a business problem, a family decision, or an artistic idea while preserving a recognizable structural role.

But the bucket still matters: its shape determines what it can receive, preserve, combine, and pour into the next bucket.

A compact Pantheon formulation:

Structure makes meaning possible. Contents make meaning actual. Use reveals whether the fit was good.

Or even tighter:

The vessel carries possibility. The filling gives it consequence.

That also gives the compiler a clean rule: don’t judge a slot by its name alone. Inspect what filled it, where that filling came from, how well it fits, and what happens when it is poured forward.